{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DepthFirstSearchEvent\/backEdge(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DepthFirstSearchEvent\/crossEdge(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DepthFirstSearchEvent\/discover(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DepthFirstSearchEvent\/finish(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DepthFirstSearchEvent\/forwardEdge(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DepthFirstSearchEvent\/treeEdge(_:)"],"title":"Enumeration Cases","anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DepthFirstSearchEvent\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DepthFirstSearchEvent\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traversal\/depthfirstsearchevent"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DepthFirstSearchEvent"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DepthFirstSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A vertex is discovered, then every edge out of it is reported once per copy, then it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"finished. An edge to an undiscovered vertex is a tree edge, and the search continues from that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex before the next edge. An edge to a vertex discovered but not yet finished is a back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge; a self-loop is one. An edge to a finished vertex is a forward edge when that vertex was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"discovered later than the edge’s source (a descendant; a repeated tree edge is one), and a cross"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge otherwise."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"What a depth-first search reports, in order, with the classification of CLRS §22.3.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DepthFirstSearchEvent"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","title":"DepthFirstSearchEvent","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DepthFirstSearchEvent"}],"modules":[{"name":"Traversal"}],"externalID":"s:9Traversal21DepthFirstSearchEventO","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SearchEvents.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Traversal\/SearchEvents.swift#L25"}},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/SQ","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/SH","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"references":{"doc://Traversal/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/s8SendableP"},"doc://Traversal